 first ingredient  I'm using Joe leeks rose silk finishing  powder with a fluffy brush from Ecotools  sometimes I actually mix regular grocery  cornstarch into it if it's going to be a  hot day and I need more oil control I've  seen a few things online about how you  can't use cornflour because it's not  specially treated or whatever but you  can use it safely  I have a blog post on it that I've  linked so you can read all about it  the next step is blush and highlighter  I love the Jacqueline Hill Becca  champagne collection palette I use the  mix of amaretto and Pamplemousse French  grapefruit blushes sorry I'm on French's  lip crap and then I put some champagne  pulp on top I'm using a real techniques  brush to apply the blush and the  highlighter I used the regular part for  blush and the cypher loominator which  I'm sure is blasphemy but I've been  reassured by true qualified makeup  artists that there are nerve rules and  makeup so but do what I want at this  point I usually realize I've put on too  much blush and blend it out with the  Ecotools brush again I'm not that  skilled at makeup  I'm using Loreal brow artist expert  mechanical brow pencil in Ebony for my  brows for the longest time it was  impossible to find a brow product that  wasn't true red for me but this new  range has greater and browns which is  awesome because it means I don't have to  buy Korean brow products online anymore  my browser micro bladed but there are a  few spots where the pigment didn't  implant well so it's a little bit patchy  mostly I just leaved them because I was  never that good at doing my brows anyway  so my slightly patchy micro bladed brows  are a million times better than my old  brows but I'm putting in effort because  I'm filming I have a really simple i  shadow process I've seen tutorials where  they really gradually put on eye shadow  and it looks amazingly blended and  gorgeous but I'm too impatient for that  I really like sleep so I like my whole  beauty routine to be like 15 minutes  long and most days I don't even use  eyeshadow so this is my quick and dirty  routine I start with a tude house proof  10 eye primer so my eyeshadow sticks on  evenly I usually go for shimmery  eyeshadow because it's a bit more  forgiving and easier to blend I'm using  the shade Venus from the Garbo and Kelly  overnight sensation palette with a real  techniques eyes shadow brush and putting  it all over my lid as the base color  then I use a pencil brush from bdellium  to add a darker shade Pandora and Pat it  on the outside corner then I used the  Real Techniques brush again and blend  the two shades together I use the clean  ish fluffy Bedell and brush to blend the  edge of the eyeshadow and heard that it  looks okay I actually got semi-permanent  eyeliner done recently after using  pencil eyeliner for about 15 years I'm  putting a little extra on here for  filming purposes and because the eye  shadow is covered up a bit but mostly  I've been just going out the door  without doing anything actually I  normally did this anyway because I do my  eyeliner and lipstick on the train I  like my sleep I don't bump anyone I  don't spread myself everywhere  no one gets eyeliner on them I'm quieter  than people talking on the phone just  let me live my life my eyeliner is from  girly cosmetics which is a makeup artist  type branch that has stalls that expose  but doesn't really sell direct I  discovered them by chance and it's been  the first pencil eyeliner that didn't  transfer on my oily lids so I've stuck  by it I'm too scared to change I don't  usually wear mascara a few people have  asked me about this it's because I have  that hair-pulling disorder that I'm  probably going to say wrong  trichotillomania and it usually happens  when I'm stressed which is quite a lot  so my eyelashes are usually too uneven  for mascara to look good once that's  done I miss my face with a setting spray  I'm currently using al Jeunesse splash  which has a really nice fine mist it  makes everything look less powdery and  more like actual human skin and  hopefully keeps it intact a bit more  during the day but I'm super oily so  usually that doesn't happen  today I'm using synergy lip flow in  TIROS I really like this lip gloss it's  more pigmented than the usual lip gloss  but it doesn't clump up it's very sticky  so it stays in place and it's really  moisturizing so that's my morning  routine I hope you found this video  interesting if you liked it and if you  want to find out more about science more  sciency stuff in this video anyway you  can look at my channel which has lots of  videos I've also got my blog which has  lots and lots of posts about beauty  science you can also follow me on  Instagram where I put lots and lots of  science-based beauty tips see you next  time  [Music]  [Music]
 

